  "verdict": "void",
  "section": "4",
  "quote": "a provision in a tenancy agreement that is inconsistent with this Act or the regulations is void",
  "reason": "Sections 25, 26, and 27 of the Act strictly limit when a landlord may enter a rental unit without notice (such as in an emergency or when the tenant consents at the time of entry). Because a blanket advance consent to enter without notice is inconsistent with these statutory rules, section 4 renders the clause void."
}

